Z||000000||Songman||04-10-2001||01:58 AM||||I can't help it.. I like this car. Don't want it to be lost in a 50 message thread and Carl not see his fine ride. I would love to build this car for real..<P>Any of you glass guys figure how hard it would be to do mods to fit the taillights? Of course, those are just computer edited Fiero taillights so we would have to find something that would actually fit..<P> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.com/tnfieros/smoothhaze.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||04-10-2001||03:32 AM||||If you build a car like that, don't park it anywhere.  It would be destroyed on any Sunday at any given shopping mall.<P>Also, the look is cool but will the novelty wear off?  Some wise guy said "form follows function."  <P>I think he meant that Fieros are beautiful because they are so tough and vise versa.  The wrap around moldings make the car look like it can take on any shopping cart.<P>Of the two styles, the rounded moldings are probably better looking than the ribbed.  But, I am a BIG fan of the '84 2m4.  That car looks like no other American car ever made. ||||reg||1
